Exit status 0, 124 lines. Every `ok` line is byte-identical to the run above: the 41 lines
starting `   ok` were extracted from each transcript and `diff` reports no difference. So the
differences between the two runs are the ones a re-run has to have -- the build took 1m 03s
instead of 0.48s because the earlier run hit a warm target directory, the binary the container
ran is 20M where 19M was recorded, and the leaf certificate expires on Oct 6 2026 rather than
Oct 4 -- and not differences in what a TLS deployment consists of.
